                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              .( Assembler )                                                                                                                  This vocabulary is imported via NEEDS ASSEMBLER or 100 LOAD     This is a Z80 adaptation of Albert van der Horst's work         available at https://github.com/albertvanderhorst/ciasdis.      In particular I carefully studied the two Forth sources         as80.frt and asgen.frt to get some clue to port his work to     be effective within a vintage Sinclair ZX Spectrum system       with Microdrive.                                                As far I can see, I used an older version that those above.     You can recognize asgen.frt in Screens between 100 and 119      and as80.frt from 120.                                                                                                          See: github.com/mattsteeldue/vforth-next/wiki/12.Assembler                                                                                                                                      .( Assembler. Use NEEDS ASSEMBLER instead )                     \ Loads ASSEMBLER vocabulary                                    NEEDS INVERT  NEEDS FLIP \ NEEDS CHECKSUM CR                    FORTH  DEFINITIONS   MARKER FORGET-ASSEMBLER \ MARKER-ASM       \ DECIMAL 139 LOAD \ check how MMU7 can be used.                VOCABULARY TOOLS-ASM IMMEDIATE                                  VOCABULARY FORTH-ASM                                            \ DECIMAL 118 LOAD \ MMU allocation ( Seems bugged )             : ASSEMBLER FORTH-ASM ; IMMEDIATE                              DECIMAL 101 LOAD \ tools                                        DECIMAL 120 LOAD \ Z80                                          DECIMAL 140 LOAD \ structure                                    DECIMAL 160 LOAD \ Z80N                                         DECIMAL 117 LOAD \ final CODE patch                             needs checksum hex E080 LP @ over - checksum .                  ." Done " CR DECIMAL                                            .( Z80 Assembler. ) CR                                          ASSEMBLER TOOLS-ASM DEFINITIONS                                 HEX           \ DP @ LP ! HEX E080 DP !                         \                                                               NEEDS INVERT  \ : INVERT -1 XOR ;                               : @+ >R R@ CELL+ R> @ ;                                         : !+ >R R@ ! R> CELL+ ;                                         : @- 0 CELL+ - >R R@ @ R> ;       