                                                                                              ( F_OPENDIR  via RST 8 hook code )                              code F_OPENDIR ( fspec -- fh f ) \ Open directory.                ex(sp)ix     \ fspec nul-terminated                             push  de|         push  bc|                                     ldn   b'|   HEX  10 N,                                          ldn   a'|   CHAR C  N,                                          di                                                              rst   08|   HEX A3       C,                                     ei                                                              ld    e'|  a|     ldn   d'|   0  N,                             exx                                                             pop   bc|         pop   de|         pop   ix|                   exx                                                             push  de|         exx                                           sbchl hl|         push  hl|                                     jpix  c;    -->                                               ( F_READDIR  via RST 8 hook code )                              code F_READDIR ( buff fspec fh -- n f ) \ Read next entry.        pop   hl|        \ file handle number                           ld    a'|   l|                                                  pop   de|        \ wildcard string (nul-terminated)             ex(sp)ix         \ buffer                                       push  bc|                                                       rst   08|   HEX A4 C,                                           jr    BACK,                                                     c;    DECIMAL                                                   0 VARIABLE FH    FH !                                         create path ," c:/tools/vforth/lib/"                            : opendir< ( -- fh )                                              bl word count over + 0 swap !                                   f_opendir 43 ?error ;                                         -->                                                             ( NextZXOS - IDE_PATH 01b1 )                                    MARKER TASK  \ M_P3DOS expects hl, de, bc, a, address                        \         returns hl, de, bc, a, errcode           : IDE_PATH ( a n -- f )                                           >R 0 0 R> $01B1 M_P3DOS >R 2DROP 2DROP R> ;                   : PATH>PAD ( -- )                                                 BL WORD COUNT >R PAD R@ CMOVE $FF PAD R> + C! ;               : PATH_OP ( b -- )                                                PATH>PAD PAD SWAP IDE_PATH 44 ?ERROR ;                        : SETCD ( -- ) 0 PATH_OP ;                                      : GETCD ( -- ) 1 PATH_OP ;                                      : MAKEDIR ( -- ) 2 PATH_OP ;                                    : REMOVEDIR ( -- ) 3 PATH_OP ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  ( DIR TEST )                                                    : DIR ( a -- )                                                    opendir< FH !                                                   begin                                                             PAD  0       1+  FH @  f_readdir  46 ?error                     while PAD ?TERMINAL IF QUIT THEN                                  begin                                                             DUP C@ ?DUP while emit 1+  \ next address                     repeat 6 emit                                                   1+        DUP @ >R                                              cell+     DUP @ >R                                              cell+     2@ SWAP 08 d.r space space                            R> .fat-date space R> .fat-time CR                          repeat                                                          FH @ F_CLOSE .                                                ;                                                               ( NextZXOS - IDE_MODE 01d5 )                                    : IDE_MODE! ( hl de bc a -- )                                     >R 0 0 R> 1                                                     [ HEX ] 01D5 M_P3DOS [ DECIMAL ]                                44 ?ERROR 2DROP 2DROP VIDEO ;                                 HEX                                                             : LAYER: <builds C, , does> dup C@   \ ide_mode!                   swap 1+ @ ide_mode! 1E emitc emitc ;                         : LAYER0 0000 IDE_MODE! ; \ ULA                                   0100 04  LAYER: LAYER10  \ Lo-Res                               0101 04  LAYER: LAYER11  \ ULA Enhanced                         0102 08  LAYER: LAYER12  \ Hi-Res                               0103 04  LAYER: LAYER13  \ Hi-Col                               0200 04  LAYER: LAYER2                                        DECIMAL                                                                                                                         ( NextZXOS - IDE_CAPACITY $01b4 )                               \ M_P3DOS expects hl, de, bc, a, address                        \         returns hl, de, bc, a as error code                   : IDE_CAPACITY ( n -- d )                                       \ n: unit (0 or 1)                                              \ d: total card capacity in sectors.                              >R  0 ( hl )   0 ( de )  R> 1 AND ( bc )  0 ( a )               [ HEX ] 01B4 M_P3DOS [ DECIMAL ]                                44 ?ERROR                                                       2DROP ( bc a ) SWAP ( hl,de )                                 ;                                                               EXIT                                                            > TEST <                                                        0 IDE_CAPACITY D.                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ( NextZXOS - DOS_FREE_SPACE $0121 )                             \ c: drive letter UpperCase                                     \ d: total card capacity in sectors.                            : DOS_FREE_SPACE ( c -- d )                                       >R  0  0  0  R>                                                 [ HEX ] 0121 M_P3DOS [ DECIMAL ]                                44 ?ERROR                                                       DROP ( a ) ROT ( de bc hl ) DROP SWAP                           \                                                             ;                                                               EXIT                                                            > TEST <                                                        CHAR C DOS_FREE_SPACE D.                                        ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ( NextZXOS - IDE_MODE 01d5 )                                    \ Set current NextBasic display mode                            : IDE_MODE! ( hl de bc a -- )                                     >R 0 0 R> 1                                                     [ HEX ] 01D5 M_P3DOS [ DECIMAL ]                                44 ?ERROR 2DROP 2DROP VIDEO                                   ;                                                               HEX                                                             : LAYER0  0000 IDE_MODE!  ;                                     : LAYER10 0100 IDE_MODE!  1E EMITC 4 EMITC ; \ Lo-Res           : LAYER11 0101 IDE_MODE!  1E EMITC 4 EMITC ; \ ULA              : LAYER12 0102 IDE_MODE!  1E EMITC 8 EMITC ; \ Hi-Res           : LAYER13 0103 IDE_MODE!  1E EMITC 4 EMITC ; \ Hi-Col           : LAYER2  0200 IDE_MODE!  1E EMITC 4 EMITC ;                                                                                                                                                    ( NextZXOS - IDE_MODE 01d5 )                                    \ Query current NextBasic display mode information              : IDE_MODE@ ( -- hl de bc a )                                     0 0 0 0                                                         [ HEX ] 01D5 M_P3DOS [ DECIMAL ]                                44 ?ERROR                                                     ;                                                               \                                                               \ hex 1840 0 800 9                                              \ hex 1820 7 800 5                                              ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                                                                                               ( DOS_FLUSH $0142 )                                             \ Flush any pending write to SD                                 : DOS_FLUSH ( c -- )                                              >R 0 0 0 R>                                                     [ HEX ] 0142 M_P3DOS [ DECIMAL ]                                44 ?ERROR                                                       DROP 2DROP                                                    ;                                                               \ CHAR C DOS_FLUSH                                              ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ( DOS_VERSION / IDE_VERSION )                                   NEEDS SPLIT                                                     : DOS_VERSION ( -- version issue )                                0 0 0 0                                                         [ HEX ] 0103 M_P3DOS [ DECIMAL ]                                44 ?ERROR                                                       2DROP NIP SPLIT                                               ;                                                               : IDE_VERSION ( -- sub ver )                                      0 0 0 0                                                         [ HEX ] 00A0 M_P3DOS [ DECIMAL ]                                44 ?ERROR                                                       2DROP NIP SPLIT                                               ;                                                               ␀                                                                                                                               ( IDE_BASIC 1/5 )                                               NEEDS ASSEMBLER                                                 CODE IDE_BASIC ( a -- f )                                         POP       HL|          \ command line address in HL             PUSH      BC|          \ save Forth registers                   PUSH      IX|                                                   LD()X     SP|  HEX 02C +ORIGIN  AA,  \ save Forth SP            LDX()     SP|  HEX 008 +ORIGIN  AA,  \ use Basic SP             LDX       DE|  HEX 5756 NN,                                     LDX       BC|  HEX 243B NN,                                     OUT(C)    D'|   INC B'|   IN(C) D'|   \ ask MMU7                DEC       B'|                                                   OUT(C)    E'|   INC B'|   IN(C) E'|   \ ask MMU6                PUSH      DE|                                                 -->                                                                                                                             ( IDE_BASIC 2/5 )                                               \ switch ROM from 3 to 2                                          LDAR                   \ ask if interrupts are enabled          PUSH      AF|                                                   DI                                                              LDX       BC|   HEX 7FFD NN,  \ port                            LDX       DE|   HEX 5B2C NN,  \ BANKM                           LDA(X)    DE|                                                   RES        4|    A|     \ switch ROM from 3 to 2                OUT(C)    A'|           \ whatever RAM page at C000             LD(X)A    DE|                                                   POP       AF|                                                   JPF       PO|  HERE 3 + AA,  \ skip EI if interrupts            EI                           \ was disabled                   -->                                                                                                                             ( IDE_BASIC 3/5 )                                                 \ prepares for ide call                                         NEXTREG  HEX 56 P, 0 N,          \ set RAM page 0 at C000       NEXTREG  HEX 57 P, 1 N,          \ set RAM page 0 at C000     \ LDX       DE|  HEX 01C0  NN,     \ IDE_BASIC via              \ RST       08|  HEX 0094  C,      \ M_P3DOS seems not work       CALL      HEX 01C0 AA,           \ direct call works            SBCHL     HL|                    \ evaluate CFlag to 0/-1     -->                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ( IDE_BASIC 4/5 )                                               \ switch ROM from 2 to 3                                          LDAR                   \ ask if interrupts are enabled          DI                                                              PUSH      AF|                                                   LDX       BC|   HEX 7FFD NN,  \ port                            LDX       DE|   HEX 5B2C NN,  \ BANKM                           LDA(X)    DE|                                                   SET        4|    A|     \ switch ROM from 2 to 3 (48K)          OUT(C)    A'|           \ whatever RAM page at C000             LD(X)A    DE|                                                   POP       AF|                                                   JPF       PO|  HERE 3 + AA,  \ skip EI if interrupts            EI                           \ was disabled                   -->                                                                                                                             ( IDE_BASIC 5/5 )                                                 POP       DE|                                                   LD        A'|   E|   \ restore MMU6                             NEXTREGA HEX 56 P,                                              LD        A'|   D|   \ restore MMU7                             NEXTREGA HEX 57 P,                                              LDX()     SP|  HEX 02C +ORIGIN  AA,  \ restore Forth SP         POP       IX|                                                   POP       BC|                                                   PUSH      HL|     \ this was obtained by SBC HL,HL above        EI                                                              NEXT                                                            C;                                                              DECIMAL                                                                                                                                                                                       ( IDE_BASIC test )                                              HEX 5C53 CONSTANT PROG                                          HEX 5C3A CONSTANT ERRNR                                         CREATE CMD_BASIC            \  ," .KEYHELP:"                    HEX F5 C, CHAR : C, F5 C,   \ PRINT:PRINT                       \ CHAR : CHAR . C, CHAR $ C,  \ .$                              CHAR : C, E2 C,             \ STOP  \  EA C,  \ REM                 0D C,  \ <CR>                                               : TEST                                                            PROG @ 6 +                                                      IDE_BASIC                                                       [ HEX ] ERRNR C@ SWAP                                         ;                                                               DECIMAL                                                         \ ÿ                                                                                                                            ( REMOUNT via IDE_MOUNT    $01d2 )                              \ M_P3DOS expects hl, de, bc, a, and address                    \         returns hl, de, bc, a, and flag error code            : REMOUNT  ( -- )                                                 BLK-FH @ F_CLOSE DROP         \ close BLOCKS file               0 0 0 0 [ HEX ] 01D2 M_P3DOS  >R 2DROP 2DROP R>                 IF                                                                ." Cannot unmount" CR                                         ELSE                                                              ." Remove/insert SD and press Y"                                BEGIN KEY UPPER [CHAR] Y = UNTIL                                0 0 0 1 [ HEX ] 01D2 M_P3DOS DROP 2DROP 2DROP                 THEN                                                            BLK-INIT [ DECIMAL ]                                          ;                                                                                                                               ( IDE_TOKENISE $01d8 )                                          \ M_P3DOS expects hl, de, bc, a, and address                    \         returns hl, de, bc, a, and flag error code            HEX                                                             : IDE_TOKENISE ( a1 n1 -- a2 n2 n3 f )                            >R 1FFF AND        \ hl=offset of text in 8K-page n             0 R> FF AND        \ c=8K-page n1, b=0 for tokenising           0 01D8 M_P3DOS NIP \ hl de bc flag                            ;                                                               : IDE_DETOKENISE ( a0 a1 n -- f )                                 >R 1FFF AND        \ hl=offset of text in 8K-page n             SWAP               \ de=addres of tokenised basic line          R> FF AND 100 +    \ c=8K-page n1, b=1 for detoken.             01D8 M_P3DOS NIP   \ hl de bc flag                            ;                                                                                                                               ( IDE_TOKENISER )                                               NEEDS HEAP  NEEDS S"  NEEDS +C                                  H" PRINT:PRINT" HEX 0D +C  \ ha                                 FAR MMU7@ IDE_TOKENISE                                                                                                          ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                                                                                               ( SPRITE structure )                                            : t                                                               #17 MMU7!                                                       $FFFF $E000                                                     do i $80 dump                                                   key drop                                                        $80 +loop                                                     ;                                                                                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                                                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ( looking for AT position in LAYERs )                           \ search memory for a specific xt for debug purposes            DECIMAL NEEDS .AT                                               : .AT                                                           22 EMITC 31 AND SWAP 21 MIN EMITC EMITC ;                       HEX                                                             : LOOK-FOR                                                        0F MMU7!                                                        FFFF  E000  DO                                                    0D 11 AT.                                                       0D11 I @ = IF I U. THEN                                         100D I @ = IF I U. THEN                                       LOOP                                                            1 MMU7! ;                                                                                                                                                                                     ( Sprite definition )                                           0                                                                 2  +FIELD  _spriteid                                            2  +FIELD  _xcoord                                              2  +FIELD  _ycoord                                              1  +FIELD  _pattern                                             1  +FIELD  _mflipflags                                          1  +FIELD  _anchor                                              1  +FIELD  _visible                                           CONSTANT SPRITE-LEN                                             \                                                               CREATE SPRITE       SPRITE-LEN  ALLOT                           -->                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ( Sprite struct definition )                                    \                                                               NEEDS ASSEMBLER                                                 NEEDS OPEN<         \ later we use as OPEN< filename.f          NEEDS J                                                         NEEDS BINARY       needs .s                                     \                                                               MARKER TASK                                                     \                                                               : db .s ."  << " ;                                              CODE WAIT halt next C;                                          : PAUSE 0 ?DO WAIT LOOP ;                                       \                                                               : +FIELD ( n1 n2 <name> -- n3 )                                   <BUILDS OVER , + DOES> @ + ;                                  -->                                                             ( Sprite struct definition )                                    0                                                                 2  +FIELD  _spriteid   \ to attr. 3 bits 5:0                    2  +FIELD  _xcoord     \ to attr. 0 + attr. 2 bit 0             2  +FIELD  _ycoord     \ to attr. 1                             1  +FIELD  _rotmir     \ to attr. 2 bits 3:1                    1  +FIELD  _pattern    \ to attr. 2 bits 7:4                    1  +FIELD  _anchor     \ to attr. 4 ...                       CONSTANT SPRITE-OB                                              \                                                               CREATE SPRITE  SPRITE-OB  ALLOT                                 -->                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ( Sprite Lib - Derek Bolli et Al. )                             BINARY 00000010 CONSTANT SPRITE-ROT                                    00000100 CONSTANT SPRITE-VFLIP                                  00001000 CONSTANT SPRITE-HFLIP                           \                                                               HEX 303B CONSTANT SPRITE-SLOT-SELECT-PORT                           0057 CONSTANT SPRITE-ATTRIBUTE-PORT                             005B CONSTANT SPRITE-PATTERN-PORT                           DECIMAL                                                            256 CONSTANT SPRITE-BUFLEN                                   \                                                               CREATE SPRITE-BUFFER SPRITE-BUFLEN ALLOT                               SPRITE-BUFFER SPRITE-BUFLEN ERASE                        -->                                                                                                                                                                                             ( Sprite Lib )                                                  \ transmit 256 bytes of sprite data from address a              \ : SPRITE-DATA>    ( a -- )                                    \ 256 OVER + SWAP DO                                            \   I C@ SPRITE-PATTERN-PORT P!                                 \ LOOP ;                                                                                                                        CODE SPRITE-DATA> ( a -- )                                        pop     hl|                                                     push    bc|                                                     ldx     bc|  SPRITE-PATTERN-PORT  NN,                           otir                                                            pop     bc|                                                     next                                                            C; -->                                                                                                                        ( Sprite Lib )                                                  \ init sprite number id                                         : SPRITE-INIT ( id -- )                                           SPRITE-SLOT-SELECT-PORT P!        \ select sprite id            SPRITE-BUFFER                                                   SPRITE-DATA>                                                  ;                                                               \ set current sprite current attribute                          : SPRITE-ATTR ( b -- )                                          \ base @ >R dup hex . dup binary . cr R> base !                   SPRITE-ATTRIBUTE-PORT P!                                      ;                                                               DECIMAL -->                                                     ␀                                                                                                                                                                                               ( Sprite Lib )                                                  \ setup up to  64 sprites read from <file>                      : SPRITE-LOAD< ( <file> -- )                                      OPEN< >R                      \ open file and save fh           064 0 DO                                                          SPRITE-BUFFER SPRITE-BUFLEN \ since we are inside a loop        J                           \ get filehandle using J            F_READ                      \ read from file                    IF      LEAVE               \ non-zero means error              ELSE    I SPRITE-INIT       \ setup this sprite                 THEN                                                            DROP             \ discard actual bytes read in any case      LOOP                                                            R>  F_CLOSE  42 ?ERROR                                        ; -->                                                                                                                           ( Sprite )                                                      HEX                                                             : SPRITE-UPDATE      ( a n -- )                                   SPRITE-SLOT-SELECT-PORT P!                                      DUP  _xcoord     C@        SPRITE-ATTR     \ attribute 0        DUP  _ycoord     C@        SPRITE-ATTR     \ attribute 1        DUP  _xcoord 1+  C@  1 AND                                      OVER _rotmir     C@ 0E AND OR                                   OVER _pattern    C@ F0 AND OR                                                              SPRITE-ATTR     \ attribute 2        DUP  _spriteid   C@ C0 OR  SPRITE-ATTR     \ attribute 3        DROP ;                                                        DECIMAL -->                                                     ␀                                                                                                                                                                                               ( Sprite )                                                      CODE SPRITE-HIDE    ( n -- )                                      exx                                                             pop     hl|                                                     ldx     bc|   SPRITE-SLOT-SELECT-PORT  NN,                      out(c)  l'|                                                     ldx     bc|   SPRITE-ATTRIBUTE-PORT    NN,                      out(c)  (hl)'|      \ Attribute 0                               out(c)  (hl)'|      \ Attribute 1                               out(c)  (hl)'|      \ Attribute 2                               out(c)  (hl)'|      \ Attribute 3                               exx                                                             next                                                            C;                                                            DECIMAL                                                         -->                                                             ( Sprite Test )                                                 \                                                               .( open<   ../../demos/NextBASIC/basicSprites/DKSprite.spr  )   \                                                               \                                                               SPRITE-LOAD< ../../demos/NextBASIC/basicSprites/DKSprite.spr    \                                                               -->                                                             ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ( Sprite Test )                                                 HEX                                                             FE 08 REG!   \ no contention on Peripeal 3 Setting              E3 14 REG!   \ Global Transparency Colour                       18 40 REG!   \ Palette Index Register                           E3 41 REG!   \ Palette Data                                     02 07 REG!   \ Go 7 MHz                                         \                                                               \ enable Sprite on Border and set Layer-Priority to SLU         \ BINARY 00000011 HEX 15 REG!                                   3 HEX 15 REG!                                                   -->                                                             ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ( Sprite definition )                                           NEEDS INVV NEEDS TRUV                                           DECIMAL                                                         \                                                                 1  SPRITE  _spriteid   !                                      009  SPRITE  _xcoord     !                                      010  SPRITE  _ycoord     !                                        0  SPRITE  _pattern    c!                                       0  SPRITE  _rotmir     c!                                       0  SPRITE  _anchor     c!                                     \                                                               SPRITE 0 SPRITE-UPDATE                                          -->                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ( TEST )                                                        \                                                               : TEST                                                            60 0 DO                                                           I 1 AND    SPRITE _spriteid !                                   I 4 *      SPRITE _xcoord !                                     SPRITE  0  SPRITE-UPDATE                                        04 pause                                                      LOOP                                                            0 SPRITE-HIDE                                                 ;                                                               ." Sync TEST "                                                  TEST                                                            -->                                                             ␀                                                                                                                               ( ISR-TEST )                                                    NEEDS INTERRUPTS                                                : ISR-TEST                                                        23672 ( FRAMES ) @ 7 AND 0= IF                                    SPRITE _xcoord @ 320 >                                          IF -20 SPRITE _xcoord ! THEN                                    5  SPRITE _xcoord  +!                                           SPRITE _xcoord @ 1 AND                                          SPRITE _spriteid !                                              SPRITE  0  SPRITE-UPDATE                                      THEN                                                          ;                                                               ISR-OFF                                                         ' ISR-TEST ISR-XT !                                             \ ISR-ON                                                        -->                                                             ( SPRITE with ISR-TEST )                                        : BYE ISR-OFF BYE ;                                             INVV CR                                                         ." GIVE ISR-OFF to stop."                                       TRUV CR                                                         \                                                                 ISR-ON                                                        \                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               needs .at  needs .paper  needs mouse                            needs ms                                                        : test                                                            begin                                                             0 0 .at mouse-xy . . CR                                         mouse-rs ?   mouse-ds ?  mouse-s ? CR                           mouse-s @ 4 + .                                                 10 ms                                                         ?terminal until                                               ;                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ( .HEX and .BIN utility )                                       DECIMAL                                                         : .HEX ( n -- ) \ print n in hexadecimal                          BASE @        \ save current base                               16 BASE !     \ set to hexadecimal                              SWAP U.       \ print number                                    BASE !                                                        ;                                                               : .BIN ( n -- ) \ print n in binary                               BASE @        \ save current base                               2 BASE !      \ set to binary                                   SWAP U.       \ print number                                    BASE !                                                        ;                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ( rshift )                                                      needs assembler                                                 code rshift ( n1 u -- n2 )                                        exx                                                             pop     bc|                                                     ld       c|  b'|                                                pop     de|                                                     bsrlde,b                                                        push    de|                                                     exx                                                             Next c;                                                       -->                                                             ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ( Lshift )                                                      needs assembler                                                 code Lshift ( n1 u -- n2 )                                        exx                                                             pop     bc|                                                     ld       c|  b'|                                                pop     de|                                                     bslade,b                                                        push    de|                                                     exx                                                             Next c;                                                       -->                                                             ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ( Enhanced ULA Control Register $43 )                              8         67 REG!     \ Palette Control (ULA first + SUL)    $43 REG@ .                                                      decimal                                                         ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ( Autoexec )                                                    \                                                                 DECIMAL                                                          8         67 REG!     \ Palette Control (ULA first + SUL)      25         64 REG!     \ Palette Index Select (blue paper)      %00000001  65 REG!     \ Palette Data (darker)                  14         64 REG!     \ Palette Index Select (yellow ink)      %11111001  65 REG!     \ Palette Data (lighter)                 1 17 EMITC EMITC       \ Paper 1 (blue)                       \                                                                 INCLUDE    /TOOLS/VFORTH/LIB/AUTOEXEC.F                         ABORT                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         ( TILEMAP study )                                                 NEEDS LAYERS                                                    NEEDS SPLIT                                                     MARKER TASK                                                   \                                                               \ 0x68 (104) - ULA Control. disable ULA output                  \ $80 $68 reg!                                                  \                                                               \ 0x6B (107) - Tilemap Control                                  \ %10100001 $6B reg!                                            -->                                                             ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                                                                                                                                                               ( TILEMAP study )                                               \ 0x6B (107) Tilemap Control                                    \ bit 7 = 1 enable the tilemap                                  \ bit 6 = 0 for 40x32, 1 for 80x32                              \ bit 5 = no attribute byte in tilemap (saves space)            \ bit 4 = select palette, 0 first, 1 second                     \ bit 3 = set text mode, i.e. 1-bit B&W bitmaps                 \ bit 2 = reserved, must be zero                                \ bit 1 = activate 512 tile mode                                \ bit 0 = force tilemap on top of ULA                           : TILE-40  %10000001 $6B reg! $80 $68 reg! ;                    : TILE-OFF %00000000 $6B reg! $00 $68 reg! ;                    : TILE-80  %11001001 $6B reg! $80 $68 reg! ;                    : SET-PAL ( c n -- ) $40 REG! $41 REG! ;                        : GET-PAL ( n -- c ) $40 REG! $41 REG@ ;                        -->                                                             ( TILEMAP study )                                               \ setup Tilemap and Definition  base addresses                  \ 40 columns, grid at $4000, 40*32*2 = 2560 = $0A00             \ definition 4bit per pixel at $4A00                            : TILE-40-BASE  \ $0A -4                                          $06 $6F reg!  \ Tile Definitions Base Address $4A00             $00 $6E reg!  \ Tilemap Base Address at $4000                 ;                                                               \ 80 columns, grid at $4000, 80*32*2 = 5120 = $1400             \ definition 1bit per pixel at $4A00                            : TILE-80-BASE  \ $14 -1                                          $13 $6F reg!  \ Tile Definitions Base Address $5400             $00 $6E reg!  \ Tilemap Base Address at $4000                 ;                                                               -->                                                                                                                             ( TILEMAP study )                                               : TILE-40-PALETTE                                                 $43 REG@        \ get current status of reg $43                 %10001111 AND                                                   %00110000 OR    \ .011.... is Tilemap 1st pal.                  $43 REG!                                                        \ 16 palette entries plus their shift                           %00000001 $01  set-pal   \ blue                                 %00000010 $02  set-pal   \ red                                  %00000011 $03  set-pal   \ magenta                              %11011000 $06  set-pal   \ yellow                               %00000001 $11  set-pal   \ blue                                 %11000000 $16  set-pal   \ red                                ; -->                                                                                                                                                                                           ( TILEMAP study )                                               : TILE-80-PALETTE                                                 $43 REG@        \ get current status of reg $43                 %10001111 AND                                                   %00110000 OR    \ .011.... is Tilemap 1st pal.                  $43 REG!                                                        \ palette entries are given in couple ink on paper              %11011000 $01  set-pal   \ yellow                               %00000001 $00  set-pal   \ on blue                              %11011011 $03  set-pal   \ white                                %00000001 $02  set-pal   \ on blue                              %11000000 $05  set-pal   \ red                                  %00000001 $04  set-pal   \ on blue                            ;                                                               -->                                                                                                                             ( TILEMAP study )                                               \ 80 columns mode, 1-bit color                                  \ Copy charset to 5400-5AFF, 1 bit remains 1 bit                \ Max 224 char defs available, we use the first 96.             \ control chars aren't stored                                   \                                                               : TILE-80-DEF                                                     $5C36 @ #256 +  \ printable only                                $5700  $5400 DO                                                   DUP C@        \ DUP 2/  OR                                      I C!                                                          