UP I * . LOOP  DROP ;        MULTIPLICATIONS    CR                                                                                                                                                                           \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 6 - Throw it for a loop         \ page 131                                                                                                                      \ rounded percent                                                 DECIMAL 822 LOAD  \ this loads R% from Screen# 822.                                                                             : COMPOUND  ( amt int -- )                                        SWAP  21 1 DO ." YEAR " I . 3 SPACES                            2DUP  R% + DUP  ." BALANCE " . CR LOOP 2DROP ;                                                                               1000 6 COMPOUND                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 6 - Throw it for a loop         \ page 131                                                        : RECTANGLE  256 0 DO I  16 MOD 0= IF                                CR THEN  ." *" LOOP ;                                    RECTANGLE   CR                                                                                                                  \ page 132                                                        : POEM   CR 11 1 DO I . ." LITTLE "                                  I 3 MOD 0= IF ." INDIANS " CR THEN LOOP                           ." INDIAN BOYS. " ;                                    POEM        CR                                                                                                                    : TABLE  CR 11 1 DO I MULTIPLICATION LOOP ;                                                                                   TABLE       CR                                                                                                                  \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 6 - Throw it for a loop                                                                           NEEDS J  NEEDS U.R                                                                                                            \ page 132                                                        : TABLE  CR 11 1 DO                                                 11 1 DO I J * 5 U.R LOOP CR LOOP ;                        TABLE    CR                                                                                                                     \ page 133                                                        : PENTAJUMPS  50 0 DO I . 5 +LOOP ;                           PENTAJUMPS    CR                                                                                                                  : FALLING  -10 0  DO I . -1 +LOOP ;                           FALLING       CR                                                                                                                \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 6 - Throw it for a loop         \ page 133                                                        : INC-COUNT   DO I . DUP +LOOP DROP ;                          1   5   0   INC-COUNT  CR                                       2   5   0   INC-COUNT  CR                                      -3 -10  10   INC-COUNT  CR                                      \ page 134                                                        : DOUBLING   32767 1 DO  I .  I +LOOP ;                       DOUBLING                                                        \ page 135                                                        : TEST 100 10 DO I . -1 +LOOP ;                               \ TEST : this system uses the latest standard DO-LOOP                                                                           \ page 136                                                        : COMPOUND   ( amt int -- )                                       SWAP 21 1 DO I . 2DUP R% + DUP . CR LOOP 2DROP ;            \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 6 - Throw it for a loop                                                                         \ page 140                                                        NEEDS U.R                                                       : R%   10 */ 5 + 10 / ;                                         : DOUBLED   6 1000  21 1  DO  CR                                    ." YEAR "  I 2 U.R                                              2DUP R% +  DUP ."   BALANCE " .                                 DUP 2000 > IF CR CR  ." MORE THAN DOUBLED IN "                                 I  . ." YEARS " LEAVE THEN                                                 LOOP 2DROP ;                                                                                    DOUBLED                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 6 - Throw it for a loop                                                                         \ Problems.                                                     \ 1. First create a word named STARS which print out n stars    \ on the same line, given n on the stack.                         : STARS   ( n -- )  0 DO  [CHAR] * EMIT  LOOP ;               10 STARS  CR                                                                                                                    \ 2. Next define BOX which prints out a rectangle of stars,     \ given width and height (number of lines), using the stack     \ order ( width height -- )                                       : BOX  ( w h -- )  0 DO CR DUP STARS  LOOP DROP ;             10 3 BOX  CR                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 6 - Throw it for a loop         \                                                               \ 3. Now create a word named \STARS which will print a          \ skewed array of stars (a rhomboid), given the height on       \ the stack. Use a DO loop and, for simplicity, make the        \ width a constant of ten stars.                                  : \STARS   ( n -- ) 0 DO CR I SPACES 10 STARS LOOP ;          3 \STARS                                                                                                                        \ 4. Now create a word which slants the stars the othe          \ direction; call it /STARS. It would take the height as        \ a stack input and use a constant of ten width. Use a DO       \ loop.                                                           : /STARS   ( n -- )                                               1- 0 SWAP DO CR I SPACES 10 STARS -1 +LOOP ;                3 /STARS                                                        \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 6 - Throw it for a loop                                                                         \ 5. Now define this last word, using a BEGIN...UNTL loop.                                                                        : A/STARS   ( n -- )                                              BEGIN                                                             CR DUP SPACES 10 STARS                                          1- DUP 0=                                                     UNTIL                                                           DROP ;                                                      ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                                                                                               \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 6 - Throw it for a loop                                                                         \ 6. Write a definition called DIAMONDS which will print out    \ the given numbe of diamonds shapes...                           : TRIANGLE  ( -- )                                                  DO                                                                CR  9 I - SPACES  I  2* 1+ STARS                              DUP +LOOP                                                       DROP ;                                                      : DIAMONDS  ( n -- )                                                0 DO                                                              1 10 0 TRIANGLE                                                -1  0 9 TRIANGLE                                               LOOP ;                                                                                                                    2 DIAMONDS                                                      \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 6 - Throw it for a loop                                                                         \ 7. Rewrite DOUBLED so that it will expect a starting          \ balance and insterest rate on the stack and will LEAVE        \ when this starting balance has doubled.                         NEEDS U.R   NEEDS 2OVER                                         : R%   10 */ 5 + 10 / ;                                         : DOUBLED   ( amt int -- )                                        OVER 2* -ROT SWAP 21 1  DO             \ 2m m n                   CR ." YEAR "  I 2 U.R 3 SPACES                                  2DUP R% +  DUP  ."   BAL " .                                    DUP 2OVER DROP > IF                                               CR CR  ." MORE THAN DOUBLED IN "                                I  . ." YEARS " LEAVE THEN                                  LOOP 2DROP DROP ;                                           1000 5 doubled                                                  \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 6 - Throw it for a loop         \ 8. Define a word called ** that will compute exponential      \ values like this:                                             \   7 2 ** .  ==>  49   (seven squared)                         \   2 4 ** .  ==>  16   (two to the fourth power)               \ For simplicity, assume positive exponent only.                  : **   ( n u -- m )                                               1 SWAP                   ( n 1 u  )                             0 ?DO                    ( n 1    )                               OVER *                 ( n m    )                             LOOP NIP ;               ( m      )                         \                                                                 7 2 ** . CR                                                     2 8 ** . CR                                                     3 0 ** . CR                                                                                                                   \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 7 - A Numbers of Kind of Numbers                                                                \ page 156                                                        : PRINTABLES   127 32 DO I EMIT SPACE LOOP ;                  PRINTABLES                                                                                                                      \ page 158                                                      7 EMIT     ( beep! )                                            ␀                                                               \ page 166                                                        : UD.   <# #S #> TYPE ;                                       12,345   UD.    CR                                              12.      UD.    CR                                              0.       UD.    CR                                              372-8493 UD.    CR                                              ␀                                                               \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 7 - A Numbers of Kind of Numbers                                                                \ page 167                                                        : .PH#   <# # # # # 45 HOLD #S #> TYPE SPACE ;                372-8493  .PH#  CR                                                                                                                : .DATE  <# # # 47 HOLD # # 47 HOLD #S #> TYPE SPACE ;        2023-08-09  .DATE  CR                                           ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                                                                                                                                                               \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 7 - A Numbers of Kind of Numbers                                                                \ page 168                                                        : SEXTAL   6 BASE ! ;                                           : :00   #  SEXTAL  #  DECIMAL 58 HOLD ;                         : SEC  <# :00 :00 #S #> TYPE SPACE ;                            60. SEC   CR                                                  1400. SEC   CR                                                  4500. SEC   CR                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 7 - A Numbers of Kind of Numbers                                                                \ page 171                                                        : .$   SWAP OVER  DABS                                              <# ROT SIGN # # 46 HOLD #S  36 HOLD #> TYPE SPACE ;                                                                        2000.00 .$  CR                                                 2,000.00 .$  CR                                                                                                                 \ the new Forth standard needs ROT before SIGN so that the      \ definition presented at page 171 won't work !                 \ \  <# # # 46 HOLD #S SIGN 36 HOLD #> TYPE SPACE ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 7 - A Numbers of Kind of Numbers                                                                \ Standard says  UM*  instead of  U*  etc.                        NEEDS M*/  NEEDS M/  NEEDS M+                                                                                                 \ page 175                                                        : %   100 M*/ ;                                               200.50 15 % D.       CR                                         200.50 15 % .$       CR                                                                                                           : R%  10 M*/ 5 M+ 10 M/ ;                                     987.65 15 R% .$      CR                                         200,000 3 1 M*/ D.   CR                                         200,000 1 4 M*/ D.   CR                                                                                                                                                                         \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 7 - A Numbers of Kind of Numbers                                                                \ page 176                                                      DECIMAL                                                                : SCORE-MORE   20 + ;                                                                                                    HEX    : SCORE-MORE   14 + ;  DECIMAL                                                                                                  : EXAMPLE  HEX 20 . DECIMAL ;                            EXAMPLE                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 7 - A Numbers of Kind of Numbers                                                                \ Problems.                                                                                                                     \ 1.  Veronica Wainwright couldn't remember the upper limit     \ for a signed single-length number, and she had no book to     \ refer to, only a Forth terminal. So she wrote a defiinition   \ called N-MAX, using BEGIN...UNTIL loop. When she executed     \ she got   32767                                               \ What was her definition ?                                                                                                      : N-MAX 0 BEGIN 1+ DUP 0< UNTIL 1- . ;                         ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 7 - A Numbers of Kind of Numbers                                                                \ 3. Write a definition that "rings" your terminal's bell       \ three times. Make sure that there is enough of delay          \ between the bells so that they are distinguishable.           \ Each time the bell rings, the word "BEEP" should appear       \ on the terminal screen.                                                                                                         : 3BELLS                                                          3 BEGIN                                                           ." BEEP " 7 7 7 EMIT EMIT EMIT                                  1- DUP WHILE                                                       30000 0 DO NOOP LOOP                                       REPEAT DROP ;                                                                                                               3BELLS                                                          \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 7 - A Numbers of Kind of Numbers                                                                \ Problems.                                                     \ 4. Rewrite the temperatur conversion definitions ...            NEEDS D-  NEEDS M*/  NEEDS M+                                   : F>C   (  F --  C )  -32.0 D+  10 18  M*/ ;                    : C>F   (  C --  F )  10 18 M*/  32.0  D+  ;                    : K>C   (  K --  C )  -273.2 M+ ;                               : C>K   (  C --  K )   273.2 M+ ;                               : F>K   (  F --  K )  F>C  C>K ;                                : K>F   (  K --  F )  K>C  C>F ;                                                                                                : .DEG   ( d -- )                                                 TUCK DABS                                                       <# # [CHAR] . HOLD #S ROT SIGN #> TYPE SPACE ;                                                                              \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 7 - A Numbers of Kind of Numbers                                                                \ Problems.                                                     \ 5.a. Write a routine which evaluates  7x^2 + 20x + 5          \ given x, and returns a double-length value.                   \ That is: x(7x +20) + 5                                          NEEDS D-  NEEDS M*/  NEEDS M+  NEEDS D<                         : DPOLY   ( n -- d )                                              DUP   7 M* 20 M+   ROT 1 M*/   5 M+ ;                                                                                       \ 5.b. How large an x will work without overflowing             \ thirty-two bits as a signed number ?                                                                                            : ?MAX-DPOLY  ( -- )                                            0  BEGIN 1+  DUP DPOLY  NIP 0< UNTIL  1- . ;                                                                                  \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 7 - A Numbers of Kind of Numbers                                                                \ Problems.                                                     \ 6. Write a word which prints the numbes 0 through 16          \ (decimal) in decimal, hexadecimal, and binary form in         \ three columns                                                                                                                   NEEDS BINARY                                                    : NUMS                                                            17 0 DO                                                           DECIMAL  ." DECIMAL "  I  2  .R  3 SPACES                       HEX      ." HEX "      I  2  .R  3 SPACES                       BINARY   ." BINARY "   I  5  .R  CR                           LOOP  DECIMAL ;                                                                                                                                                                             \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 7 - A Numbers of Kind of Numbers                                                                \ Problems                                                      \ 8. Write a definition for phone-number formatting word        \ that will also print the area code with a slash if and        \ only if the number includes an area code. E.g.                \ 555-1234     .PH#  555-1234                                   \ 213/372-8493 .PH#  213/372-8493                                                                                                 : .PH#  ( d -- )                                                  <# # # # # [CHAR] - HOLD # # #                                     OVER IF [CHAR] / HOLD #S THEN #> TYPE SPACE ;                                                                            \ 555.1234     .PH# \  555-1234                                 \ 213.372.8493 .PH# \  213/372-8493                                                                                             \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays                                                                \ page 183                                                        VARIABLE  DATE                                                12  DATE !                                                                                                                      \ page 184                                                      DATE @ . CR                                                     DATE ?   CR                                                                                                                     13  DATE !                                                      DATE ?   CR                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays                                                                \ pag 184                                                         VARIABLE DATE  VARIABLE MONTH  VARIABLE YEAR                    : !DATE  ( month day year -- )                                    YEAR !  DATE !  MONTH ! ;                                   7 31 23 !DATE                                                                                                                     : .DATE   MONTH ?   DATE ?   YEAR ?  ;                        .DATE                                                           ␀                                                               \ : DECIMAL   10 BASE ! ;                                       \ : HEX       16 BASE ! ;                                       \ : OCTAL      8 BASE ! ;                                       \ : BINARY     2 BASE ! !                                                                                                       \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays                                                                \ page 188                                                        VARIABLE EGGS                                                   : RESET   0 EGGS !  ;                                           : EGG     1 EGGS +! ;                                                                                                         \ page 189                                                      RESET                                                           EGG                                                             EGG                                                             EGG                                                             EGGS ?                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays                                                                \ page 190                                                        200 CONSTANT LIMIT     \ LIMIT is an user variable, so you                             \ get a warning message that warns                              \ you about that.                                                                                        : ?TOO.HOT  LIMIT > IF ." DANGER -- REDUCE HEAT " THEN ;      201 ?TOO.HOT CR                                                                                                                 ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                                                                                               \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays                                                                  NEEDS 2VARIABLE                                                                                                               \ page 193                                                        2VARIABLE DATE                                                800,000  DATE 2!                                                DATE 2@ D.    CR                                                                                                                \ from previous chapter                                           : .DATE  <# # # 47 HOLD # # 47 HOLD #S #> TYPE SPACE ;                                                                        7/16/23  DATE 2!                                                DATE 2@ .DATE     CR                                                                                                                                                                            \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays\ page 193                                                        NEEDS 2CONSTANT                                                 200,000  2CONSTANT  APPLES                                    APPLES @ D.    CR                                                                                                               \ page 194                                                        400,000  2CONSTANT  MUCH                                        : MUCH-MORE   MUCH D+  ;                                      APPLES MUCH-MORE D.     CR                                                                                                        355 113  2CONSTANT PI                                         10000 PI */ .           CR                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays\ page 196                                                        VARIABLE LIMITS  8 ALLOT                                      220 LIMITS     !                                                340 LIMITS  2+ !                                                \ page 198                                                        : LIMIT   2* LIMITS ! ;                                       170  2 LIMIT !                                                                                                                    : ?TOO.HOT  ( burner# temp -- )                                   LIMIT @ >  IF ." DANGER -- REDUCE HEAT " THEN ;             210  0 ?TOO.HOT   CR                                            230  0 ?TOO.HOT   CR                                            310  1 ?TOO.HOT   CR                                            250  1 ?TOO.HOT   CR                                            \ etc.                                                          \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays                                                                  NEEDS U.R    NEEDS PAGE    NEEDS DUMP                                                                                         \ page 199                                                        VARIABLE COUNTS  10 ALLOT                                       COUNTS 12 ERASE                                                                                                                 : RESET     COUNTS  12 ERASE ;                                  : COUNTER   2*  COUNTS + ;                                      : TALLY     COUNTER 1  SWAP +! ;                                                                                              -->                                                             \ --> definition allows continuing LOADing the next Screen                                                                                                                                      \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays\ page 200                                                        : CATEGORY DUP 18 < IF 0 ELSE                                              DUP 21 < IF 1 ELSE                                              DUP 24 < IF 2 ELSE                                              DUP 27 < IF 3 ELSE                                              DUP 30 < IF 4 ELSE  5                                           THEN THEN THEN THEN THEN SWAP DROP ;               \ page 201                                                        : LABEL    DUP  0= IF ." REJECT "      ELSE                                DUP 1 = IF ." SMALL "       ELSE                                DUP 2 = IF ." MEDIUM "      ELSE                                DUP 3 = IF ." LARGE "       ELSE                                DUP 4 = IF ." EXTRA LARGE " ELSE                                THEN THEN THEN THEN THEN DROP ;                    -->                                                             \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays                                                                \ page 201                                                      1 LABEL    CR                                                                                                                     : EGGSIZE   CATEGORY DUP LABEL TALLY ;                        23 EGGSIZE  CR                                                                                                                  \ page 202                                                        : REPORT   PAGE ." QUANTITY    SIZE " CR CR                       6 0 DO  I COUNTER @ 5 U.R                                               7 SPACES I LABEL CR LOOP ;                          REPORT                                                                                                                          COUNTS 12 DUMP                                                                                                                  \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays                                                                \ page 207                                                        CREATE LIMITS  220 , 340 , 170 , 100 , 190 ,                                                                                    CREATE SIZES  18 C,  21 C,  24 C,  27 C,  30 C,  255 C,                                                                         : CATEGORY   ( n1 -- n2 )                                         6 0 DO                                                            DUP SIZES I + C@ <                                              IF                                                                DROP I LEAVE                                                  THEN                                                          LOOP ;                                                      ␀                                                               ␀                                                               \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays                                                                \ Problems.                                                     \ 1. a) Write two words called BAKE-PIE and EAT-PIE.            \ The 1st word increases the number of available PIES by one    \ The 2nd decreases the number by 1 and thanks you for the pie  \ but if there is no pie, it types "What pie?"                                                                                    CREATE PIES 0 ,                                                 : BAKE-PIE  1 PIES +! ;                                         : EAT-PIE  PIES @  IF ." THANK YOU " -1 PIES +!                                  ELSE ." WHAT PIE? "  THEN ;                  EAT-PIE      CR                                                 BAKE-PIE     CR                                                 EAT-PIE      CR                                                 ␀                                                               \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays␀                                                               \ Problems.                                                     \ 1. b) Write a words called FREEZE-PIES which takes all the    \ pies availale and adds them to the number of pies in the      \ freezer. Remember that frozen pies cannot be eaten.           ␀                                                                 CREATE FROZEN-PIES 0 ,                                          : FREEZE-PIES  PIES @ FROZEN-PIES +! 0 PIES ! ;                                                                               BAKE-PIE BAKE-PIE FREEZE-PIES     CR                            PIES ?                            CR                            FROZEN-PIES ?                     CR                            ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays                                                                \ Problems.                                                     \ 3. Define a word called .BASE which prints the current        \ value of the variable BASE in decimal. Test it by first       \ changing BASE to some value other than ten.                                                                                     : .BASE                                                           BASE @ DUP                                                      DECIMAL .                                                       BASE ! ;                                                                                                                    DECIMAL .BASE       CR                                          HEX .BASE           CR                                          ␀                                                                                                                               \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays\ 3. Define a number-formatting word called M. which prints     \ a double-length number with a decimal point. The position     \ of the decimal point within the number is movable and         \ depends on the value of a variable you will define as         \ PLACES  for example, if you store a 1 into PLACES, you          will get  200,000 M.  20000.0 ok                              \ that is, with the decimal point one place from the right.     \ A zero in PLACES should produce no decimal point at all.        VARIABLE PLACES    1 PLACES !                                   : M.   ( d -- )  SWAP OVER DABS <#                                    PLACES @ ?DUP IF 0 DO # LOOP [CHAR] . HOLD THEN                 #S   ROT   SIGN  #>  TYPE SPACE ;                                                                                       0 PLACES ! 200,000 M.    CR                                     1 PLACES ! 200,000 M.    CR                                     \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays\ 4. In order to keep track of the inventory of colord          \ pencils in your office, create an array, each cell of         \ which contains the count of different colored pencils.        \ Define a set of words so that, for exmple, the phrase         \  RED PENCILS                                                  \ return the address of the cell that contains the count of     \ red pencils etc...                                              : ENUMERATED   ( n -- ) 0 DO I [COMPILE] CONSTANT LOOP ;        4 ENUMERATED     RED  BLUE  GREEN  ORANGE                       CREATE #PENCILS   23 ,  15 ,   12 ,     0 ,                     : PENCILS   ( n -- a )  2*  #PENCILS + ;                                                                                      RED  PENCILS  @ .    CR                                         BLUE PENCILS  @ .    CR                                                                                                         \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays\ 5. A histogram is a graphic representation of a series of     \ vaues. Each value is shown by the height or length of a       \ bar. In this exercise you will create an array of values      \ and print a histogram which displays a line of "*"s for       \ each value. First create an array with about ten cells.       \ Initialize each element with a value in the range 0 - 60      \ On each line print the number of the cell followed by a       \ number of "*"s equal to the content of that cell.                                                                               NEEDS U.R                                                       CREATE 'SAMPLES   11 ,  2 ,  5 ,  3 ,  3 ,  2 ,                                   15 , 21 ,  3 ,  8 , 10 ,  0 ,  3 ,            : STARS ( n -- ) 0 ?DO [CHAR] * EMIT LOOP ;                     : SAMPLE ( n -- a ) 2* 'SAMPLES + ;                             : PLOT 11 0 DO CR I 2 U.R SPACE I SAMPLE @ STARS LOOP CR ;    \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 8 - Variables, Constants, Arrays\ 6. Tic-tac-toe ...                                              CREATE BOARD  9 ALLOT  : CLEAR  BOARD 9 ERASE ;  CLEAR          : BOARD@   ( n -- c )  BOARD + C@ ;                             : BOARD!   ( b n -- )  BOARD + C! ;                             : .HORIZ   DUP 2- 3 MOD 0=  SWAP  6 < AND                                  IF CR ." --|---|-- " CR THEN ;                       : .VERT    3 MOD   IF [CHAR] | EMIT SPACE THEN ;                : DISPLAY     CR 9 0 DO                                             I .VERT  I BOARD@  ?DUP                                         IF 1+ 2/ 9 * [CHAR] O + ELSE BL THEN                            EMIT SPACE I .HORIZ                                           LOOP ;                                                        : X!  ( n -- ) 1-   1  SWAP BOARD! DISPLAY ;                    : O!  ( n -- ) 1-  -1  SWAP BOARD! DISPLAY ;                                                                                  \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 9 - Under the Hood                                                                                NEEDS SEE                                                                                                                       801 LOAD   ( Load GREET from ch. 1 )                                                                                            SEE GREET                                                                                                                     \ page 215                                                        ' GREET EXECUTE                                                                                                                 VARIABLE POINTER                                                ' GREET POINTER !                                               POINTER @ EXECUTE                                                                                                                                                                             \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 9 - Under the Hood                                                                              \ page 217                                                        : HELLO     ." HELLO " ;                                        : GOODBYE   ." GOODBYE " ;                                      VARIABLE 'ALOHA                                                 : ALOHA  'ALOHA @ EXECUTE ;                                   CR                                                                                                                              ' HELLO   'ALOHA !                                              ALOHA  CR                                                                                                                       ' GOODBYE 'ALOHA !                                              ALOHA  CR                                                                                                                                                                                       \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 9 - Under the Hood              \ page 218                                                      \ Here we adhere to FORTH Inc. standard                           : SAY    '   'ALOHA !  ;                                                                                                      SAY HELLO                                                       ALOHA      CR                                                                                                                   SAY GOODBYE                                                     ALOHA      CR                                                                                                                     : COMING   ['] HELLO    'ALOHA ! ;                              : GOING    ['] GOODBYE  'ALOHA ! ;                            COMING   ALOHA    CR                                            GOING    ALOHA    CR                                                                                                            \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 9 - Under the Hood                                                                              \ page 219                                                        SEE INTERPRET     CR CR                                                                                                       \ page 228                                                        SEE QUIT          CR CR                                                                                                       \ page 233                                                        SEE HERE          CR CR                                       ␀                                                               \ page 234         