                             ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 9 - Under the Hood              \ Problem 1.                                                    \ First review Chap. 2, Prob. 6.  Without changing any of       \ those definitions, now write a word called COUNTS which       \ will allow the judge to optionally enter the numbe of         \ counts for any crime. For instance the entry                  \ CONVICTED-OF BOOKMAKING 3 COUNTS TAX-EVASION WILL-SERVE       \   ==>  17 YEARS                                               \ will compute the sentence for one count of bookmaking and     \ three counts of tax evasion.                                    MARKER TASK  DECIMAL 814 LOAD                                   : COUNTS  ( n -- )                                                ' -ROT 0 DO OVER EXECUTE LOOP NIP ;                         CONVICTED-OF BOOKMAKING                                         3 COUNTS TAX-EVASION                                            WILL-SERVE                                                      \ Brodie - Starting FORTH - Ch. 9 - Under the Hood              ␀                                                               \ Problem 2. What is the beginning of your private dictionary ? \ COLD    \ we don't have EMPTY yet.                            \ HERE U.                                                       ␀                                                               \ Problem 3. In your system, how far is the pad from the top    \ of your private dictionary ?                                    PAD HERE - U.                                                                                                    