                                             \                                                               code uart-get-block ( a n -- )                                    di                                                              exx                                                             pop     de|   \ number of bytes                                 pop     hl|   \ memory address                                  ldx     bc|   uart-rx-port  nn,                               \                                                               -->                                                                                                                             ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - protocol )                           here                                                              in(c)   a'|                                                     ora      a|                                                     jrf     z'|   holdplace                                           ld   (hl)'|   a|                                                incx    hl|                                                 here disp,                                                        decx    de|                                                     ld      a'|   d|                                                ora      e|                                                     jrf    nz'|   back,                                             exx                                                             ei                                                              next                                                          c;                                                              ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - protocol )                           sh . go                                                         test                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - protocol )                           code uart-get-block ( a -- )                                    hex f3 c, d9 c,       \ di   exx                                    d1 c, e1 c,       \ pop  de    pop  hl                          01 c, 143B ,      \ ld   bc,   uart-rx-port  nn,                ed c, 78 c,       \ in   a,(c)                                  b7 c,             \ or   a                                      28 c, 02 c,       \ jr   z,$+2                                  77 c, 23 c,       \ ld (hl),a  inc hl                           1b c,             \ dec  de                                     7a c, b3 c,       \ ld   a,d   or e                             20 c, f4 c,       \ jr   nz,$-12                                d9 c, fb c,       \ exx  ei                                     dd c, e9 c,       \ jp(ix)                                  smudge decimal                                                                                                                  ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - protocol )                           code halt                                                       hex 76 c,        \ halt                                             dd c, e9 c,  \ jp (ix)                                      smudge decimal                                                  \                                                               : test                                                            begin                                                             halt halt                                                       $4000 #64  erase                                                bl uart-wait-b \ wait for BL to sync                            $4000 #64  uart-get-block                                       ?terminal                                                     until                                                         ;                                                               ␀                                                               ( trim routine )                                                needs assembler                                                 code ltrim  ( a1 -- b )                                           exx                                                             ldhl()  $5C0B  AA, \ DEFADD                                     ldx   bc|  4  NN,   addhl bc|                                   ld    e'|  (hl)|                                                incx  hl|                                                       ld    d'|  (hl)|                                                incx  hl|                                                       ld    c'|  (hl)|                                                incx  hl|                                                       ld    b'|  (hl)|                                                exdehl                                                          addhl bc|                                                     -->                                                             ( trim routine )                                                  decx  hl|                                                       ldn   a'|  BL  N,                                             here                                                              cpd                                                             jrf   z'|  BACK,                                                incx  bc|                                                       push bc|                                                        exx                                                             next                                                            c;                                                            ␀                                                               ␀                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ( RPI0 wrapper )                                                needs RPi0                                                      : this ( -- a n )                                                 >in @ >R   -2 >in +!  [compile] \                               blk @ if    blk @ 1-     if    r@ c/l 1- and c/l swap -                                  else  b/buf c/l -   then                                        else  span @  then                     blk @ if  blk @ block  else  tib @  then  R> + swap ;         : send ( a1 n1 a2 n2 -- n3 )                                      2dup      uart-send-text  uart-wait-for                                   uart-send-cr    uart-wait-cr-lf                       uart-rx-burst 7 -  0 max ;                                    : ask  pad 1024 this send ;                                     : sh  here 1024 this send drop ;                                : display cr pad swap type cr ;                                                                                                 ( RPI0 wrapper )                                                needs RPi0                                                      : ask  ( -- n )                                                   >in @ >R   -2 >in +!  [compile] \                               blk @ if    blk @ 1-     if    r@ c/l 1- and c/l swap -                                  else  b/buf c/l -   then                                        else  span @  then                     blk @ if  blk @ block  else  tib @  then  R> + swap           \                                                                 2dup      uart-send-text  uart-wait-for                         pad 100   uart-send-cr    uart-wait-cr-lf                       uart-rx-burst 7 -  0 max ;                                    : sh ( -- )                                                       ask drop ;                                                                                                                                                                                    ( RPI0 wrapper )                                                  needs s"  needs ask  needs sh                                 \ RPi0-init                                                     \ uart-wait-prompt                                                send echo 'print 2**300' > temp.py                              ask  python temp.py                                             pad swap type                                                 \                                                               : test                                                            here 200                                                        s"  python -c 'print 2**400'  "                                 send here swap type                                           ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               ( RPI0 wrapper )                                                \ RPi0-init                                                                                                                     \ uart-wait-prompt                                                send echo 'print 2**300' > temp.py                              ask  python temp.py                                             pad swap type                                                 \                                                                 ask  python -c 'print 2**400'                                   pad swap type                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 ( Example for THIS definition )                                 \                                                                 ASK     echo $BASH_VERSION                                      DISPLAY                                                       \                                                                 ASK     date                                                    DISPLAY                                                       \␀                                                              \ ASK     date -s 2024-07-13                                    \ ASK     date -s 17:30                                         \ 2DROP                                                         \                                                                 ASK     date                                                    DISPLAY                                                       ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ( UART Raspberry PI Zero )                                      \ hex 300 6633 ! \ 7 emit pitch                                 \                                                               NEEDS LAYERS                   NEEDS BCOPY                      NEEDS TRUV    NEEDS INVV                                        NEEDS ASSEMBLER                                                 \ NEEDS INTERRUPT␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀\                                                               MARKER DONE                                                     \                                                               HEX 5C08 CONSTANT LASTK          \ system variable                  143B CONSTANT UART-RX-PORT                                      133B CONSTANT UART-TX-PORT                                      153B CONSTANT UART-CT-PORT                                  -->                                                                                                                             ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - setup )                              \ Table of actual clock speeds depending on video mode          \ These are double precision integers you can read with 2@      HERE                                                            DECIMAL \ values are divided by 100 to better handle them         28.0000   , ,   \ Base VGA timing   28 MHz                      28.5714   , ,   \ VGA setting 1     28.571.429 Hz               29.4643   , ,   \ VGA setting 2     29.464.286 Hz               30.0000   , ,   \ VGA setting 3     30 MHz                      31.0000   , ,   \ VGA setting 4     31 MHz                      32.0000   , ,   \ VGA setting 5     32 MHz                      33.0000   , ,   \ VGA setting 6     33 MHz                      27.0000   , ,   \ Digital           27 MHz                    CONSTANT SYS-CLK-ARY                                            DECIMAL -->                                                                                                                     ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - setup )                              HEX                                                             \ compute actual clock speed depending on video mode            : SYS-CLOCK ( -- d )                                              11 REG@ 7 AND          \ Video timing register: 0-7             4 * SYS-CLK-ARY + 2@   \ fetch from array created before      ;                                                               \ send 14-bits prescalar to UART receive port                   \ prescalar = sysclock / baudrate                               : UART-SET-PRESCALAR ( n -- )                                     DUP                                                             7F AND UART-RX-PORT P!      \ send low 7 bits of 14 bits        7 RSHIFT                    \ presclar                          80  OR UART-RX-PORT P!      \ send high 7 bits of 14 bits     ;                                                               DECIMAL -->                                                     ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - setup )                              DECIMAL                                                         \ compute prescalar to be used with previous definition         : UART-BAUD-TO-PRESCALAR ( d -- n )                               100 M/          \ divide BAUD by 100 to able to handle it       SYS-CLOCK       \ obtain actual system clock speed / 100        ROT M/                                                        ;                                                               \ usage is: 115200. UART-SET-BAUDRATE                           : UART-SET-BAUDRATE ( d -- )                                      UART-BAUD-TO-PRESCALAR                                          UART-SET-PRESCALAR                                            ;                                                               DECIMAL -->                                                                                                                     ␀                                                               ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - setup )                              HEX                                                             \ Select Raspberry PI Zero UART and set Baudrate                \                                                               : PI0-SELECT  ( d -- )                                            40 UART-CT-PORT P!    \ select PI Zero UART control port        UART-SET-BAUDRATE     \ uses double integer param               30 A0 REG!            \ PI Pheripeal enable                   \ 91 A2 REG!            \ PI I2S Audio control                  ;                                                               DECIMAL -->                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - transmit )                           HEX                                                             \ non-zero when transmitter is busy sending a byte              : ?UART-BUSY-TX ( -- f )                                          UART-TX-PORT P@   \ UART TX port                                02 AND            \ bit is set when busy                      ;                                                               \ There is no transmit buffer so program must make sure the     \ last transmission is complete before sending another byte     : UART-TX ( b -- )                                                BEGIN                                                             ?UART-BUSY-TX  0=  ?TERMINAL OR                               UNTIL                                                           UART-TX-PORT P!         \ Transmit                            ;                                                               DECIMAL -->                                                     ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - transmit )                           DECIMAL                                                         \ Utilities                                                     \                                                               : UART-SEND-EOT ( -- )   \ End Of Transmission                    04 UART-TX                                                    ;                                                               \                                                               : UART-SEND-ETX ( -- )   \ End of TeXt                            03 UART-TX                                                    ;                                                               DECIMAL -->                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     ␀                                                               ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - receive )                            HEX                                                             : ?UART-BYTE-READY  ( -- f )  \ non zero when byte ready          UART-TX-PORT  P@  1 AND                                       ;                                                               : UART-RX  ( -- b | 0 )       \ accept a byte                     UART-RX-PORT  P@                                              ;                                                               : UART-WAIT ( b -- )     \ wait for a specific byte or Break      BEGIN                       \ b                                   UART-RX OVER =            \ b f                                 ?TERMINAL OR              \ b f                               UNTIL DROP                  \                                 ;                                                               DECIMAL -->                                                                                                                     ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - receive )                            \ wait for a byte with timeout in ms                            : UART-RX-TIMEOUT ( n -- c | 0 )                                  0 SWAP                      \ 0 n                               1+ 0                        \ 0 n+1 0                           DO                          \ 0                                   ?UART-BYTE-READY IF       \ 0                                     UART-RX                 \ 0 b                                   SWAP DROP               \   b                                   LEAVE                   \   b                                 THEN                      \ 0                                   NOOP                      \      minimum delay                LOOP                        \ 0                               ;                                                               DECIMAL -->                                                                                                                     ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - receive )                            HEX                                                             : UART-WAIT-READY                                                 BEGIN                                                             ?UART-BYTE-READY ?TERMINAL OR                                 UNTIL                                                         ;                                                               \ simple wait for a specific string "SUP> "                     : UART-WAIT-PROMPT  ( -- )                                        [CHAR] S UART-WAIT                                              [CHAR] U UART-WAIT                                              [CHAR] P UART-WAIT                                              [CHAR] > UART-WAIT                                                    BL UART-WAIT                                            ;                                                               DECIMAL -->                                                     ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - receive a block )                    \ Accept from I/O  up to n bytes and store them at a.           CODE UART-RX-BURST ( t a n -- )                                      di                                                              pop     DE|                   \ length counter                  Exx                                                             pop     hl|                   \ address                         pop     de|                   \ timeout                         ldx     bc|  UART-TX-PORT  NN,  \ 133Bh                    HERE                               \              a1                 decx    de|                   \ check timeout      \ 6          ld      a'|  d|                                    \ 4          ora      e|                                        \ 4          jrf     z'|  HOLDPLACE        \              a1 a2 \ 7          -->                                                                                                                        ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - receive a block )                         in(c)   a'|                  \ bit 0               \ 12         rra                          \ non-zero when ready \  4         jrf    nc'|  1 PICK BACK,    \ back to a1          \  7         inc     b'|                  \ RX port 143Bh       \  4         ini                          \ bc goes 133Bh       \ 16         ld      a'| (hl)|                                  \  4         anda     a|                  \ check for 0x00      \  4         jrf     z'|  HOLDPLACE       \            a1 a2 a3 \  7         exX                                                \  4         Decx    DE|                  \ dec length counter  \  6         Ld      A'|  D|                                    \  4         Ora      E|                  \ check for zero      \  4         Exx                                                \  4    -->                                                                                                                             ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - receive a block )                    \ At 115200 Bauds bit duration is 8.68  micro-seconds           \ a 512 bytes-buffer is filled in less than 4.45 ms.            \ The 512 bytes burst-read takes 56832 T-states                 \ plus enter-exit time that at 28 MHz is about 2.03 ms          \ so we emtpy the buffer  2 times faster than it fills up.      \                                                                    jrf    nz'|  1 PICK BACK,     \ repeat until done  \ 10    HERE DISP,    \ a3                                              HERE DISP,    \ a2                                                   DROP     \ a1                                                   exx                                                             ei                                                              jpix                                                            C;  -->                                                                                                                    ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - receive a block )                    HEX                                                             \                                                               CODE  DIS-INT                                                     F3 C,             \ di                                          DD C, E9 C,       \ jp (ix)                                   SMUDGE                                                          \   UART-TX-PORT P@ 1 AND                                       CODE  ENA-INT                                                     FB C,             \ di                                          DD C, E9 C,       \ jp (ix)                                   SMUDGE                                                          \                                                               DECIMAL -->                                                                                                                                                                                     ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - receive a block )                    DECIMAL                                                         : UART-RX-CHUNK ( t a n -- )                                      DIS-INT                          \ t a n                        ROT 0 DO                         \ a n                            UART-TX-PORT P@ 1 AND IF       \ a n f   wait ready               SWAP UART-RX-PORT P@         \ n a b   accept byte              ?DUP 0= IF LEAVE THEN        \ n a b   0x00 quits               OVER C! 1+ SWAP 1-           \ a n     store & incr             DUP 0= IF LEAVE THEN         \ a n     decr counter           THEN                                                          LOOP                             \ a n                          2DROP                            \                              ENA-INT                                                       ;                                                               DECIMAL -->                                                     ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - block receive )                      DECIMAL                                                         \ receive 1K to Screen n                                        : UART-RECEIVE    ( n -- )                                        B/SCR * DUP 1+ SWAP                                             BLOCK B/BUF -1 UART-RX-CHUNK                                    BLOCK B/BUF -1 UART-RX-CHUNK                                  ;                                                               \ prepare Screen # n to accept data from UART burst read        : UART-SCREEN  ( n -- )                                           B/SCR *       DUP 1+                                            BLOCK B/BUF BLANK                                               BLOCK B/BUF BLANK                                             ;                                                               DECIMAL -->                                                     ␀                                                               ( UART Raspberry PI Zero - send a command )                     \ send a string                                                 HEX                                                             : UART-SEND ( a n -- )                                            BOUNDS DO                                                         I C@ UART-TX                                                  LOOP                                                            0D UART-TX                                                    ;                                                               \                                                               HERE                                                            ," perl --help"                                                 CONSTANT CMD                                                    DECIMAL -->                                                     ␀                                                                                                                               ( UART Raspberry PI Zero )                                      -->                                                             ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ( UART Raspberry PI Zero )                                      -->                                                             ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                                                               ␀                  